# paper/ holds the JSTOR scan of Simon (1955), a copyrighted Biometrika article.
# Only its provenance record is shipped. Every printed cell the analysis rests
# on is transcribed in data/printed_tables.csv with its page locator.
paper/*
!paper/PROVENANCE.md

# Page renders of the 1955 article (copyrighted), used for transcription.
results/pages/

# Third-party scans and OCR layers: Davis (1941), Lotka (1926), Eldridge (1911),
# Zipf (1949), and two renders of the Models of Man (1957) reprint. URL,
# retrieval date, byte size and SHA-256 of each are in data/raw/MANIFEST.csv;
# the double-entered transcriptions are in data/sources/ and
# data/reprint_1957_models_of_man.csv. Project Gutenberg #4300 is public domain
# and is shipped.
data/raw/*
!data/raw/MANIFEST.csv
!data/raw/gutenberg4300/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Atelier working files (see README, "Working files not in this repository")
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The control-plane stub: orients an AI agent inside the owner's private project
# tracker and carries absolute paths into it.
AGENTS.md

